    detailedContent: "Dr. Rajesh Kanna's session is a lifeline for students navigating the financial aspects of postgraduate education. With tuition costs being a significant consideration, this session ensures that every deserving student is aware of the financial support mechanisms available at Christ University and beyond.\n\nThe session categorizes available scholarships into five tiers:\n\n1. University Merit Scholarships: Based on CGPA performance at the end of each semester. Top performers in each batch receive fee waivers ranging from 25% to 100%. The criteria, selection process, and historical data on recipients are shared.\n\n2. Need-Based Financial Aid: For students demonstrating financial hardship. The application process requires documentation of family income, and the Financial Aid Committee evaluates requests on a case-by-case basis.\n\n3. Alumni Endowment Scholarships: Funded by successful alumni, these scholarships target specific criteria — first-generation college students, students from rural backgrounds, or those excelling in specific technical domains.\n\n4. External Scholarships: Dr. Kanna provides a curated list of government and private scholarships that Christ University students are eligible for, including INSPIRE (DST), UGC Junior Research Fellowships, state government merit scholarships, and corporate-sponsored education grants.\n\n5. Research Assistantships: For students interested in research, faculty members offer stipend-based assistantships where students contribute to ongoing research projects while earning financial support.\n\nThe session includes practical guidance on application writing — how to craft a compelling scholarship essay, gather the right documentation, and meet deadlines. Common mistakes that lead to rejection are highlighted, and templates are provided.",
