    detailedContent: "Akshay Singhal's session brings the professional world directly into the orientation classroom. As an MCA alumnus from the 2021-23 batch — a recent graduate who still remembers the orientation jitters — his insights are uniquely relatable and immediately actionable.\n\nAkshay begins with his personal story: how he chose MCA at Christ University, the challenges he faced in his first semester (especially adapting to the pace of postgraduate coursework), the projects that defined his skill development, and the pivotal moments that led to his current role as Analytics Manager at a leading data company.\n\nThe data analytics landscape is explored through Akshay's professional lens: what companies are actually looking for versus what job descriptions say, which certifications genuinely matter (Google Data Analytics, Azure DP-900, Tableau), and how to build a portfolio of data projects that demonstrates real competence.\n\nThe alumni network advantage is a key theme. Akshay explains how the Christ University alumni community operates — LinkedIn groups, WhatsApp channels, annual alumni meets, and informal mentorship connections. He shares specific examples of how alumni referrals have helped recent graduates land interviews at companies that don't typically visit the campus.\n\nPractical interview preparation advice covers: how to crack analytics case studies, SQL proficiency requirements, Python for data manipulation (Pandas, NumPy), visualization tools (Tableau, Power BI), and the often-overlooked importance of business acumen and communication skills in analytics roles.\n\nThe session includes a live Q&A where students ask about salary expectations, work-life balance in analytics, remote work trends, and how to decide between data analytics, data engineering, and data science career paths.",
