    detailedContent: "The Collaboration & Creativity workshop is the capstone technical event of the orientation program, bringing the real world into the classroom through industry collaboration. Pod.ai (an AI-focused product company) and Neostats (a data analytics firm) provide actual problem statements from their business operations, and students work in teams to develop solutions within a half-day sprint.\n\nThe morning begins with presentations from industry representatives:\n- Pod.ai introduces their problem statement: a natural language processing challenge related to customer intent classification. Students must design an approach to categorize customer queries into actionable categories using available data.\n- Neostats presents a data analytics challenge: analyzing a dataset to identify patterns, generate insights, and create a dashboard that tells a compelling data story.\n\nStudents are divided into teams of 5-6, deliberately mixing MCA and MSc AIML students to encourage cross-pollination of skills. Each team receives:\n- The problem statement with supporting data\n- Access to cloud computing resources\n- A mentor (either an industry expert or senior student) for guidance\n- A presentation template for the final showcase\n\nThe workshop follows a modified Scrum methodology:\n- Sprint Planning (30 min): Teams analyze the problem, divide tasks, and create a basic roadmap.\n- Sprint 1 (90 min): Core development and analysis work.\n- Stand-up Review (15 min): Quick status check and obstacle identification.\n- Sprint 2 (60 min): Refinement, testing, and presentation preparation.\n- Demo Day (45 min): Each team presents their solution to a panel of industry judges and faculty.\n\nThis format gives students their first taste of agile project delivery, cross-functional teamwork, and the pressure of presenting work to industry stakeholders. The best team's solution may be considered for actual implementation by the partner company — adding real stakes to the exercise.\n\nFeedback from industry mentors is detailed and constructive, covering technical approach, teamwork dynamics, presentation quality, and business relevance of the proposed solutions.",
